    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that’s the thing... there are no new paths. the people i know, the career i was building, it was all based on that specific thing. without it, i’m just a shell. everyone else is moving forward and i’m just standing here with a bunch of useless knowledge that doesn't even matter anymore. it feels like the version of me that actually mattered is just dead.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes sense that you feel like a shell when your entire identity was built on a foundation that has crumbled, and the pain of realizing your knowledge might be \"useless\" is a heavy burden to carry alone. You are right that the version of you that was defined by that specific success is gone, but that doesn't mean the person underneath is useless or that there is no way forward. Sometimes the only way to stop feeling like a hollow shell is to let go of the expectation of who you were supposed to be and allow yourself to simply exist without the pressure of being productive.",
